<title>USA: Unisource Worldwide Q1 net falls.</title>
<headline>Unisource Worldwide Q1 net falls.</headline>
<dateline>VALLEY FORGE, Pa. 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>UNISOURCE WORLDWIDE, INC.</p>
<p>				   FINANCIAL SUMMARY</p>
<p>		   (in thousands, except earnings per share)</p>
<p>					 Three Months Ended December 31</p>
<p>					 1996	1995	  % Change</p>
<p> Revenues		    $1,728,533 $1,716,165	     0.7%</p>
<p> Income from Operations	45,104     50,187	   (10.1)</p>
<p> Net Income			20,151     26,229		---</p>
<p> Pro Forma Net Income (A)	 ---     23,970		---</p>
<p> Earnings Per Share (B)	  0.30	 0.35	   (15.9)</p>
<p> Shares Outstanding (C)	67,576     67,576		---</p>
<p>(A)  Includes additional pro forma interest expense of $3.7 million ($2.3 million net of tax), which assumes that the spin-off of Unisource occurred on October 1, 1995.</p>
<p>(B)  Earnings Per Share has been calculated using the actual net income for the current year and pro forma net income for the prior year.</p>
<p>(C)  Represents actual outstanding Unisource common shares as of December 31, 1996 (&quot;Spin-off&quot; date) plus the dilutive effect of stock options.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk +1 212 859 1610))</p>
